<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila okays 27 bln peso Mitsubishi auto project.</title>
<headline>Manila okays 27 bln peso Mitsubishi auto project.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' Board of Investments (BOI) said on Monday it had approved a 26.99 billion peso auto part manufacturing plant, 90 percent owned by Mitsubishi Electric Co and Mitsubishi Corp.</p>
<p>The company, Laguna Auto Parts Manufacturing Corp, will make and export an anti-skid brake system-pulse generator, which acts as a wheel speed sensor in cars.</p>
<p>It expects to start commercial operation by June.</p>
<p>Projects approved by BOI are eligible for tax and tariff incentives.</p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8938, fax 817-6267</p>
</text>
